1
00:03:21,818 --> 00:03:27,818
Inside every one of us is a special talent waiting to
come out. The trick is finding it.

2
00:06:43,636 --> 00:06:49,636
Billy Elliot is a drama, comedy, music film directed by Stephen Daldry.

3
00:10:05,454 --> 00:10:11,454
County Durham, England, 1984.

4
00:13:27,272 --> 00:13:33,272
The miners' strike has started and the police have started coming up from
Bethnal Green, starting a class war with the lower classes suffering.

5
00:16:49,090 --> 00:16:55,090
Caught in the middle of the conflict is 11-year old Billy Elliot, who, after leaving his boxing club
for the day, stumbles upon a ballet class and finds out that he's naturally talented.

6
00:20:10,909 --> 00:20:16,909
He practices with his teacher Mrs.

7
00:23:32,727 --> 00:23:38,727
Wilkinson for an upcoming audition in Newcastle-upon Tyne
for the royal Ballet school in London.

8
00:26:54,545 --> 00:27:00,545
Billy Elliot, played by Jamie Bell.

9
00:30:16,363 --> 00:30:22,363
Jackie Elliot, played by Gary Lewis.

10
00:33:38,181 --> 00:33:44,181
Mrs Wilkinson, played by Julie Walters.

11
00:37:00,000 --> 00:37:06,000
Grandma, played by Jean Heywood.

12
00:40:21,818 --> 00:40:27,818
Tony Elliot, played by Jamie Draven.

13
00:43:43,636 --> 00:43:49,636
Michael Caffrey, played by Stuart Wells.

14
00:47:05,454 --> 00:47:11,454
Billy Elliot is a 2000 British coming-of-age drama film
directed by Stephen Daldry and written by Lee Hall.

15
00:50:27,272 --> 00:50:33,272
Set in County Durham in North East England during the 1984–1985 miners' strike,
the film is about a working-class boy who has a passion for ballet.

16
00:53:49,090 --> 00:53:55,090
His father objects, based on negative stereotypes of male ballet dancers.

17
00:57:10,909 --> 00:57:16,909
The film stars Jamie Bell as 11-year-old Billy, Gary Lewis as his father, Jamie
Draven as Billy's older brother, and Julie Walters as his ballet teacher.

18
01:00:32,727 --> 01:00:38,727
Adapted from a play called Dancer by Lee Hall,
development on the film began in 1999.

19
01:03:54,545 --> 01:04:00,545
Around 2,000 boys were considered for the role of Billy before Bell was chosen.

20
01:07:16,363 --> 01:07:22,363
Filming began in the North East of England in August 1999.

21
01:10:38,181 --> 01:10:44,181
Greg Brenman and Jon Finn served as producers, while
Stephen Warbeck composed the film's score.

22
01:14:00,000 --> 01:14:06,000
Billy Elliot is a co-production among BBC Films, Tiger
Aspect Pictures and Working Title Films.

23
01:17:21,818 --> 01:17:27,818
The film premiered at the 2000 Cannes Film Festival,  and began a wider theatrical release in the United
Kingdom on 29 September 2000 by Universal Pictures through United International Pictures.

24
01:20:43,636 --> 01:20:49,636
Billy Elliot received positive critical response and commercial success,
earning $109.3 million worldwide on a $5 million budget.

25
01:24:05,454 --> 01:24:11,454
At the 54th British Academy Film Awards, the film won
three of thirteen award nominations.

26
01:27:27,272 --> 01:27:33,272
Jamie Bell became the youngest winner of Best Actor in a Leading Role.

27
01:30:49,090 --> 01:30:55,090
The film also earned three nominations at the 73rd Academy Awards for Best
Director, Best Original Screenplay and Best Actress in a Supporting Role.

28
01:34:10,909 --> 01:34:16,909
In 2001, the film was adapted as a novel by Melvin Burgess.

29
01:37:32,727 --> 01:37:38,727
The story was also adapted for the West End stage as Billy
Elliot the Musical, first produced in 2005.

30
01:40:54,545 --> 01:41:00,545
It opened in Australia in 2007 and on Broadway in New York City in 2008.

31
01:44:16,363 --> 01:44:22,363
The film explores themes of dancing, friendship,
dreams, dancing class, northern england.

32
01:47:38,181 --> 01:47:44,181
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
